{
  "id": "COMPOUND:31899 - PROTEIN:5788",
  "verbalization": "Nortoxiferine, dihydro- is implicated in the biological pathway leading to SNB-78 through a series of target relationships, all centered on the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. This subunit serves as a common target for multiple compounds, including Nortoxiferine, which is linked to Hex-3-en-1-yl 2-methylbut-2-enoate and Diplotrin A. These compounds, in turn, target SNB-78, suggesting a potential mechanism involving the regulation of proteasome activity. The evidence suggests that Nortoxiferine may modulate the proteasome through interactions with its regulatory subunit, which could influence the degradation of proteins involved in cellular processes that ultimately affect SNB-78. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Nortoxiferine in modulating proteasome function, which may have implications for its biological effects on SNB-78.",
